{"id": "EUVD-2026-66460", "enisaUuid": "9fb88b5d-0d1d-38c4-aca9-fc6b55b06d78", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/zcrypt: Improve EP11 CPRB length and overflow checks\n\nThe xcrb_msg_to_type6_ep11cprb_msgx() function lacks proper input\nvalidation, creating security vulnerabilities:\n1. Missing minimum size validation: The ep11_cprb structure and\n   subsequent payload fields (pld_tag, pld_lenfmt) are copied from\n   userspace without verifying sufficient buffer length.\n2. Arithmetic overflow in length calculations: CEIL4 alignment could\n   overflow, bypassing size checks and enabling buffer overflows.\n3. The payload is asn1 encoded but the function just uses a simple c\n   struct overlay to access some fields of the payload.\n\nFix by using size_t for length calculations, adding U32_MAX boundary\nchecks after alignment, and validating minimum request size and\nminimum reply size before copying from userspace. Do a very simple\nasn1 parsing of the payload up to the function value field.", "datePublished": "2026-08-26T14:37:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:28", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f463f474773aa49ed1d6087d95d44cea7099fdc7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2976b9d2e716c7e5487ca7c29a7bd076cf9adf08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17ac0bc866fc624cd05f022dcd8b730c0af11bb1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5h39-f843-4g5v", "CVE-2026-80545"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a924aa5-89a5-3b2f-bd25-9ce56232c525", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "17b47dc4-065d-315d-ba57-a6200cc76661", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.10"}, {"id": "2b0c9b74-bd42-30ab-a77d-8f3137913f07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9da85d4780515f65983e0af151458599adaef3d"}, {"id": "3a2ea7fb-70da-3f00-b6fd-39d01a334063", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "c220a70f-8642-31e1-8dbf-eda3150d85e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2c6d91eb8b1533753755f07803e47eceed263d0 <17ac0bc866fc624cd05f022dcd8b730c0af11bb1"}, {"id": "c7f52bda-d147-3c94-a401-157bc10b54b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2c6d91eb8b1533753755f07803e47eceed263d0 <2976b9d2e716c7e5487ca7c29a7bd076cf9adf08"}, {"id": "d96aaabe-6483-3147-b423-40e72c8f9081", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.114 <6.13"}, {"id": "e2c26729-f614-38c5-b569-f8af3131384d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "20b0b0159390fa5c00a435195649680fefda81e0 <f463f474773aa49ed1d6087d95d44cea7099fdc7"}, {"id": "ee549b55-bf8f-3ac3-98e7-83453fa012cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4b6f67a9-1acd-3d7f-9aaa-09790c1669cb", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}